{"id":"mahabharata-5-174","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":174,"title":"चतुःसप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 174 · Hotravahana, Amba's grandfather","summary":{"en":"The ascetics debate what Amba should do, and her maternal grandfather, the royal sage Hotravahana, arrives and recognizes her. Amba asks how her bitter sorrow may be ended, and he tells her to seek Parashurama.","kn":"ಅಂಬೆ ಏನು ಮಾಡಬೇಕೆಂದು ತಪಸ್ವಿಗಳು ಚರ್ಚಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅವಳ ತಾಯಿಯ ತಂದೆ ರಾಜರ್ಷಿ ಹೋತ್ರವಾಹನನು ಬಂದು ಅವಳನ್ನು ಗುರುತಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತನ್ನ ಕಹಿ ದುಃಖ ಹೇಗೆ ಕೊನೆಗೊಳ್ಳುವುದೆಂದು ಅಂಬೆ ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ ಪರಶುರಾಮನನ್ನು ಆಶ್ರಯಿಸೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"तपस्वी विचार करते हैं कि अम्बा को क्या करना चाहिए, और उसके नाना, राजर्षि होत्रवाहन, आकर उसे पहचान लेते हैं। अम्बा पूछती है कि उसका कटु दुःख कैसे समाप्त हो, और वे उसे परशुराम की शरण लेने को कहते हैं।","te":"అంబ ఏమి చేయాలో తాపసులు చర్చిస్తారు; ఆమె తాతగారు రాజర్షి హోత్రవాహనుడు వచ్చి ఆమెను గుర్తిస్తాడు. తన తీవ్ర దుఃఖం ఎలా తీరుతుందని అంబ అడగగా పరశురాముని ఆశ్రయించమని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"அம்பை என்ன செய்ய வேண்டும் என்று தவசிகள் விவாதிக்க, அவள் தாய்வழித் தாத்தா ராஜரிஷி ஹோத்ரவாஹனன் வந்து அவளை அடையாளம் காண்கிறான். தன் கசப்பான துயர் எப்படித் தீரும் என்று அம்பை கேட்க, பரஶுராமரை நாடுமாறு சொல்கிறான்.","ml":"അംബ എന്തുചെയ്യണമെന്ന് താപസന്മാർ ചർച്ച ചെയ്യുന്നു; അവളുടെ മാതൃപിതാവായ രാജർഷി ഹോത്രവാഹനൻ എത്തി അവളെ തിരിച്ചറിയുന്നു. കയ്പേറിയ ദുഃഖം എങ്ങനെ അവസാനിപ്പിക്കാമെന്ന് അംബ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; പരശുരാമനെ സമീപിക്കാൻ അദ്ദേഹം അവളോട് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.174; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्ते तापसाः सर्वे कार्यवन्तोऽभवंस्तदा ।\nतां कन्यां चिन्तयन्तो वै किं कार्यमिति धर्मिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all those ascetics, concerned for that maiden, wondered, being righteous men, what should be done."}},{"n":2,"text":"केचिदाहुः पितुर्वेश्म नीयतामिति तापसाः ।\nकेचिदस्मदुपालम्भे मतिं चक्रुर्द्विजोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some ascetics said she should be taken to her father's house; some of the best of the twice-born thought to reproach us."}},{"n":3,"text":"केचिच्छाल्वपतिं गत्वा नियोज्यमिति मेनिरे ।\nनेति केचिद्व्यवस्यन्ति प्रत्याख्याता हि तेन सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some thought Shalva's king should be approached and made to take her; others said no, for he had rejected her."}},{"n":4,"text":"एवं गते किं नु शक्यं भद्रे कर्तुं मनीषिभिः ।\nपुनरूचुश्च ते सर्वे तापसाः संशितव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Things being so, they said again, good lady, what can the wise do? All those ascetics of strict vows spoke."}},{"n":5,"text":"अलं प्रव्रजितेनेह भद्रे शृणु हितं वचः ।\nइतो गच्छस्व भद्रं ते पितुरेव निवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enough of renunciation here, good lady; hear this good advice: go from here to your father's house, and may it be well with you."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रतिपत्स्यति राजा स पिता ते यदनन्तरम् ।\nतत्र वत्स्यसि कल्याणि सुखं सर्वगुणान्विता ।\nन च तेऽन्या गतिर्न्याय्या भवेद्भद्रे यथा पिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever your father, the king, decides next, you will live there happy, with every good quality; no other refuge is right for you, good lady, than your father."}},{"n":7,"text":"पतिर्वापि गतिर्नार्याः पिता वा वरवर्णिनि ।\nगतिः पतिः समस्थाया विषमे तु पिता गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A woman's refuge is her husband or her father, fair lady; her husband when things are even, and her father when they are not."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रव्रज्या हि सुदुःखेयं सुकुमार्या विशेषतः ।\nराजपुत्र्याः प्रकृत्या च कुमार्यास्तव भामिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Renunciation is very hard, especially for a delicate princess and unmarried girl like you, fair lady."}},{"n":9,"text":"भद्रे दोषा हि विद्यन्ते बहवो वरवर्णिनि ।\nआश्रमे वै वसन्त्यास्ते न भवेयुः पितुर्गृहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are many dangers, good lady, to you living in a hermitage that would not be in your father's house."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततस्तु तेऽब्रुवन्वाक्यं ब्राह्मणास्तां तपस्विनीम् ।\nत्वामिहैकाकिनीं दृष्ट्वा निर्जने गहने वने ।\nप्रार्थयिष्यन्ति राजेन्द्रास्तस्मान्मैवं मनः कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those Brahmins told the ascetic woman: seeing you alone in this lonely, dense forest, kings will seek you; so do not set your mind on this."}},{"text":"अम्बोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Amba said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"न शक्यं काशिनगरीं पुनर्गन्तुं पितुर्गृहान् ।\nअवज्ञाता भविष्यामि बान्धवानां न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot go back to the city of Kashi, to my father's house; I will surely be despised by my relatives."}},{"n":12,"text":"उषिता ह्यन्यथा बाल्ये पितुर्वेश्मनि तापसाः ।\nनाहं गमिष्ये भद्रं वस्तत्र यत्र पिता मम ।\nतपस्तप्तुमभीप्सामि तापसैः परिपालिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ascetics, I lived in my father's house as a child, but I will not go to live where my father is; I wish to practice austerity, guarded by ascetics."}},{"n":13,"text":"यथा परेऽपि मे लोके न स्यादेवं महात्ययः ।\nदौर्भाग्यं ब्राह्मणश्रेष्ठास्तस्मात्तप्स्याम्यहं तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So that in the next world too I may not suffer such great misfortune, best of Brahmins, I will practice austerity."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"इत्येवं तेषु विप्रेषु चिन्तयत्सु तथा तथा ।\nराजर्षिस्तद्वनं प्राप्तस्तपस्वी होत्रवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While those Brahmins were pondering in this way and that, the royal sage and ascetic Hotravahana arrived in that forest."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततस्ते तापसाः सर्वे पूजयन्ति स्म तं नृपम् ।\nपूजाभिः स्वागताद्याभिरासनेनोदकेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the ascetics honored the king with welcome and the like, a seat and water."}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्योपविष्टस्य ततो विश्रान्तस्योपशृण्वतः ।\nपुनरेव कथां चक्रुः कन्यां प्रति वनौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he was seated and rested, the forest dwellers began again to speak of the maiden."}},{"n":17,"text":"अम्बायास्तां कथां श्रुत्वा काशिराज्ञश्च भारत ।\nस वेपमान उत्थाय मातुरस्याः पिता तदा ।\nतां कन्यामङ्कमारोप्य पर्याश्वासयत प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the story of Amba and the Kashi king, Bharata, her mother's father rose trembling, took the girl on his lap and comforted her."}},{"n":18,"text":"स तामपृच्छत्कार्त्स्न्येन व्यसनोत्पत्तिमादितः ।\nसा च तस्मै यथावृत्तं विस्तरेण न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He asked her to tell fully the origin of her trouble from the start, and she told him in detail all that had happened."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः स राजर्षिरभूद्दुःखशोकसमन्वितः ।\nकार्यं च प्रतिपेदे तन्मनसा सुमहातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the royal sage, of great austerity, was filled with sorrow and grief, and took up her cause in his mind."}},{"n":20,"text":"अब्रवीद्वेपमानश्च कन्यामार्तां सुदुःखितः ।\nमा गाः पितृगृहं भद्रे मातुस्ते जनको ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trembling, he said to the afflicted and deeply suffering girl: do not go to your father's house, good lady, for I am your mother's father."}},{"n":21,"text":"दुःखं छेत्स्यामि तेऽहं वै मयि वर्तस्व पुत्रिके ।\nपर्याप्तं ते मनः पुत्रि यदेवं परिशुष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will cut your grief; stay with me, daughter. Your heart is enough burdened, daughter, that you waste away like this."}},{"n":22,"text":"गच्छ मद्वचनाद्रामं जामदग्न्यं तपस्विनम् ।\nरामस्तव महद्दुःखं शोकं चापनयिष्यति ।\nहनिष्यति रणे भीष्मं न करिष्यति चेद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go at my word to Rama, son of Jamadagni, the ascetic; Rama will remove your great sorrow and grief, and he will kill Bhishma in battle if he does not do as he says."}},{"n":23,"text":"तं गच्छ भार्गवश्रेष्ठं कालाग्निसमतेजसम् ।\nप्रतिष्ठापयिता स त्वां समे पथि महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go to that best of the Bhargavas, with the splendor of the fire of time; the great ascetic will set you on a level path."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततस्तु सस्वरं बाष्पमुत्सृजन्ती पुनः पुनः ।\nअब्रवीत्पितरं मातुः सा तदा होत्रवाहनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, weeping aloud again and again, she said to her mother's father Hotravahana:"}},{"n":25,"text":"अभिवादयित्वा शिरसा गमिष्ये तव शासनात् ।\nअपि नामाद्य पश्येयमार्यं तं लोकविश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bowing my head, I will go at your command; may I see today that noble one, famed in the world."}},{"n":26,"text":"कथं च तीव्रं दुःखं मे हनिष्यति स भार्गवः ।\nएतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुमथ यास्यामि तत्र वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"How will that Bhargava end my fierce sorrow? I wish to hear this, and then I will go there."}}]}]}